7	 *   <li>{@code REGION} — the region code derived from the postcode/city (see {@link OwnerRegion}),
8	 *       an upper-case letter run (NSW, VIC, QLD or UNKNOWN);</li>
9	 *   <li>{@code FY} — the 2-digit fiscal year (the last two digits of the fiscal year's start-year,
10	 *       the same {@code YY} as the owner's {@code fiscalYear});</li>
11	 *   <li>{@code HASH8} — the first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over
12	 *       (normalizedTelephone + lastName), the same HASH8 used by the region-and-hash identity;</li>
13	 *   <li>{@code CHK} — a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of
14	 *       {@code <REGION><FY><HASH8>}.</li>
15	 * </ul>
16	 *
17	 * <p>This replaces the former separate {@code customerCode}, {@code membershipNumber} and standalone
18	 * {@code checkDigit}: the region, fiscal year, audit record and owner segment now all read the
19	 * memberId. Collision de-duplication (appending {@code -<n>}) is applied to the whole memberId, so a
20	 * de-duplicated value may carry a trailing {@code -<n>} suffix; the parse helpers below tolerate it
21	 * by reading the region and fiscal year from the leading segments.
22	 */
